D is wrong. This is net working capital, not the ratio.
P6-04  Answer B. The cash flow ratio is operating cash flow over current liabilities.
A is wrong. That is the cash ratio, without marketable securities.
C is wrong. Net income is not used.
D is wrong. Free cash flow and total liabilities are a different measure.
